WEBVTT

00:00:01.390 --> 00:00:02.980
Jinko!

00:00:02.980 --> 00:00:05.790
First-years! Don't let them beat you!

00:00:05.790 --> 00:00:07.480
You can do it!

00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:11.990
Jinko

00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:11.990
Saeki Maijo

00:00:09.990 --> 00:00:11.990
Good game!

00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:15.450
You knocked us sideways.

00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:16.570
Good game.

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:18.510
"Knocked us sideways"?

00:00:18.510 --> 00:00:20.450
Th-Thanks.

00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:22.960
It was a fine game.

00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:25.670
Score! We won!

00:00:25.670 --> 00:00:28.170
We've gotten <i>crazy</i> strong!

00:00:28.170 --> 00:00:29.500
It's bonkers.

00:00:28.870 --> 00:00:31.310
Yeah, totally bonkers.

00:00:31.310 --> 00:00:33.010
Seriously bonkers...

00:02:13.630 --> 00:02:18.630
<b>Episode 21 
Good Luck Charm</b>

00:02:14.260 --> 00:02:16.990
Don't let it go to your heads.

00:02:17.570 --> 00:02:20.530
I don't remember going 
so easy on you in training

00:02:20.530 --> 00:02:22.960
that two consecutive victories

00:02:22.960 --> 00:02:26.000
in a couple of practices games 
would be cause for celebration.

00:02:27.250 --> 00:02:29.750
It's only natural for you 
to try to win everything.

00:02:30.280 --> 00:02:33.100
But we don't know if our opponents
have the same mindset.

00:02:34.510 --> 00:02:38.260
One or two victories here
doesn't prove that you've gotten better.

00:02:39.400 --> 00:02:43.260
Winning isn't the aim of games played 
during this summer training camp.

00:02:44.220 --> 00:02:45.820
Like I told you before,

00:02:45.820 --> 00:02:52.400
these games are for figuring out
which plays work and which ones don't.

00:02:53.740 --> 00:02:54.520
First-years!

00:02:56.240 --> 00:03:00.330
Your movements during the Maijo game
weren't too bad.

00:03:01.970 --> 00:03:06.790
All of you will play in 
our remaining six games.

00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:09.910
There won't be any time for slacking.

00:03:09.910 --> 00:03:11.670
Prepare yourselves.

00:03:11.670 --> 00:03:12.790
Yes, sir.

00:03:14.680 --> 00:03:16.250
Thanks for the food.

00:03:16.250 --> 00:03:17.490
Thank you.

00:03:17.490 --> 00:03:19.700
We'll be heading to the field at one.

00:03:20.230 --> 00:03:21.650
Get some rest.

00:03:21.650 --> 00:03:24.940
Excuse me. Could I get a glass of water?

00:03:26.800 --> 00:03:30.060
Yoshida-sensei, are you okay?

00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:31.850
Ah, yes...

00:03:32.320 --> 00:03:37.190
Are you sure I didn't do 
anything strange yesterday?

00:03:38.020 --> 00:03:40.690
I can't remember a thing.

00:03:40.690 --> 00:03:42.520
Not particularly.

00:03:44.230 --> 00:03:47.330
Futami-san had a great time.

00:03:50.680 --> 00:03:51.690
I'm sleepy.

00:03:51.690 --> 00:03:53.150
Yoshida here.

00:03:51.970 --> 00:03:53.850
Let's head to our room.

00:03:53.850 --> 00:03:55.080
Bed, bed...

00:03:54.220 --> 00:03:55.080
Yes.

00:03:55.080 --> 00:03:56.340
What?

00:03:56.340 --> 00:03:59.380
Sorry. I hung them all outside.

00:03:56.340 --> 00:04:01.340
Y-Yes. Yes, I understand.

00:03:59.380 --> 00:04:01.340
What?

00:04:02.160 --> 00:04:03.490
Goodbye.

00:04:06.850 --> 00:04:08.970
Jinko

00:04:08.930 --> 00:04:10.850
Ogi Tech

00:04:17.150 --> 00:04:19.610
Go, Noka!

00:04:19.610 --> 00:04:21.610
Pass the ball around!

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:40.550
We lost.

00:04:41.490 --> 00:04:43.110
This sucks.

00:04:43.110 --> 00:04:45.260
It's not like we were too cocky out there...

00:04:45.260 --> 00:04:48.540
But he's definitely going to 
yell at us before dinner.

00:04:49.050 --> 00:04:50.890
Crap...

00:04:50.890 --> 00:04:53.790
Dammit, we lost!

00:04:53.790 --> 00:04:55.820
It's frustrating, isn't it?

00:04:55.820 --> 00:04:58.050
I'm not even tired yet!

00:05:03.900 --> 00:05:06.440
Hey, Tree Trunk. What's that?

00:05:07.630 --> 00:05:09.690
Oh! That's the thing everyone's
 been talking about...

00:05:11.280 --> 00:05:11.700
Bingo.

00:05:12.100 --> 00:05:17.730
Ta-da! It's not a punching machine,
but a tackling machine.

00:05:17.210 --> 00:05:19.710
<b>200 yen per tackle</b>

00:05:17.730 --> 00:05:21.630
Apparently, everyone who comes to 
Sugadaira has a go on it at least once.

00:05:22.210 --> 00:05:26.800
Sugadaira's probably the only 
place in the world that has one.

00:05:27.270 --> 00:05:30.660
Wow! A tackling machine, huh?

00:05:30.660 --> 00:05:32.720
Let's give it a try, Tree Trunk.

00:05:32.720 --> 00:05:33.800
What?

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:37.020
As long as we're here,
let's have a go on it again this year.

00:05:37.020 --> 00:05:38.230
Yeah.

00:05:38.230 --> 00:05:40.610
I want to go back and eat!

00:05:41.150 --> 00:05:42.220
Okay...

00:05:42.220 --> 00:05:43.730
Hey.

00:05:43.730 --> 00:05:45.740
It's Sumiaki and Kenji.

00:05:46.190 --> 00:05:48.280
Hey, it's Keijo!

00:05:48.280 --> 00:05:50.120
Miyuki-kun, good to see you again.

00:05:50.120 --> 00:05:53.320
Yeah, we haven't seen you 
since our joint practice.

00:05:53.320 --> 00:05:54.240
You're right.

00:05:56.000 --> 00:05:59.800
Sekizan! I missed you!

00:06:01.040 --> 00:06:04.490
We heard you beat a team
that made Osaka's quarters.

00:06:04.490 --> 00:06:05.630
Yeah.

00:06:05.630 --> 00:06:09.050
Not bad. I was impressed 
when I heard the news.

00:06:10.540 --> 00:06:13.560
By the way, we just watched Ryoin play.

00:06:13.560 --> 00:06:15.830
They've got another strong team this year.

00:06:16.310 --> 00:06:17.640
Ryoin...

00:06:26.320 --> 00:06:29.820
Kanagawa's gonna be really
competitive again this year.

00:06:26.630 --> 00:06:29.820
Goes without saying...

00:06:29.820 --> 00:06:33.980
But Keijo will be the last team standing!

00:06:31.870 --> 00:06:33.980
What's all this ruckus?

00:06:33.980 --> 00:06:35.330
Keijo?

00:06:35.330 --> 00:06:37.280
Jinko's with them.

00:06:37.280 --> 00:06:39.730
Well, if it isn't Sagami!

00:06:39.730 --> 00:06:41.580
You guys seem to be doing well, too.

00:06:41.930 --> 00:06:44.060
Yeah, thankfully.

00:06:44.060 --> 00:06:46.630
What are you guys doing together?

00:06:47.190 --> 00:06:49.210
M-Miyuki Atsushi!

00:06:50.590 --> 00:06:52.180
Ow!

00:06:52.180 --> 00:06:53.980
I'll get you someday!

00:06:54.930 --> 00:06:57.050
Huh? Is this for me?

00:06:57.050 --> 00:06:59.180
Hana's such a weird guy.

00:06:57.730 --> 00:06:59.180
Thanks.

00:06:59.180 --> 00:07:01.060
Dammit!

00:07:04.650 --> 00:07:06.020
Huh?

00:07:06.020 --> 00:07:08.940
You'll pay for that!

00:07:11.860 --> 00:07:14.710
Hey, let's hold a tackling contest.

00:07:15.330 --> 00:07:17.580
I'll go first!

00:07:19.330 --> 00:07:21.330
Score

00:07:21.330 --> 00:07:22.580
How was that?

00:07:22.580 --> 00:07:24.210
Good job, Kenji.

00:07:24.210 --> 00:07:25.740
Not really.

00:07:25.740 --> 00:07:30.090
That one doesn't count. 
Let's establish some rules first.

00:07:30.090 --> 00:07:33.020
How about each school picks three
to represent them,

00:07:30.090 --> 00:07:35.350
<b>1 Game  1 Tackle</b>

00:07:30.090 --> 00:07:35.350
<b>Once the buzzer sounds, 
tackle the bag within 10 seconds. 
The second buzzer indicates 
the end of the round.
 Always tackle using your right shoulder.</b>

00:07:33.020 --> 00:07:35.350
and the highest total score wins?

00:07:35.730 --> 00:07:37.340
No objections here.

00:07:37.340 --> 00:07:39.220
Yeah, let's do it.

00:07:39.220 --> 00:07:42.000
If Sekizan's playing, I'm playing.

00:07:42.000 --> 00:07:46.320
Since there are only three of us, 
we'll all have to participate.

00:07:46.320 --> 00:07:47.600
Good idea.

00:07:47.600 --> 00:07:49.530
I'd like to gather some data. Let's join in.

00:07:50.220 --> 00:07:51.950
Fine.

00:07:52.360 --> 00:07:54.480
Keijo will start.

00:07:54.480 --> 00:07:58.450
The world's greatest hooker: 
Taira Tadakazu...

00:07:58.450 --> 00:08:02.080
And here he goes!

00:08:02.710 --> 00:08:04.960
Score

00:08:02.710 --> 00:08:04.960
All right!

00:08:04.960 --> 00:08:07.510
How was that, Sekizan?

00:08:07.510 --> 00:08:08.550
He's so annoying.

00:08:08.550 --> 00:08:10.530
You're next, Sagami. Who're you sending?

00:08:11.150 --> 00:08:12.490
Goshozome, you go.

00:08:12.490 --> 00:08:14.510
Okay, I'll throw in a tackle.

00:08:16.510 --> 00:08:18.010
Score

00:08:18.010 --> 00:08:21.430
What? Keijo beat you.

00:08:21.430 --> 00:08:24.270
There weren't any girls cheering me on.

00:08:24.630 --> 00:08:26.430
We'll send...

00:08:26.430 --> 00:08:28.000
Sekki, why don't you go?

00:08:28.000 --> 00:08:28.890
Okay, gotcha.

00:08:35.700 --> 00:08:37.950
Score

00:08:35.700 --> 00:08:37.950
Sekki, nice!

00:08:37.950 --> 00:08:40.650
I can't believe you matched my score.

00:08:40.650 --> 00:08:41.830
I'm delighted.

00:08:41.830 --> 00:08:43.960
I really want to redo mine...

00:08:44.530 --> 00:08:47.140
We'll send Miyuki.

00:08:51.710 --> 00:08:53.220
<b>Score</b>

00:08:53.760 --> 00:08:56.590
Kenji, I beat you.

00:08:56.940 --> 00:08:59.550
What? Let me try again.

00:08:59.550 --> 00:09:01.310
Ken-chan, you can't go twice.

00:09:09.400 --> 00:09:11.270
Oops, sorry.

00:09:11.270 --> 00:09:13.280
What are you doing, Hachi-senpai?

00:09:13.280 --> 00:09:15.290
At least he scored higher than Gion-kun...

00:09:14.240 --> 00:09:16.740
<b>Tacchan: What's up?
Me: Looks like they're having a tackle machine contest.
Tacchan: Sounds fun.
Me: Check out the tackle maniac's score.</b>

00:09:17.500 --> 00:09:19.480
I'll take our last go.

00:09:21.650 --> 00:09:24.910
All right! Nice one, Hisakawa!

00:09:24.910 --> 00:09:26.850
Our last man is Wada.

00:09:26.850 --> 00:09:28.200
We're counting on you.

00:09:28.200 --> 00:09:29.130
Sure.

00:09:32.470 --> 00:09:34.820
Over 200, huh?

00:09:34.820 --> 00:09:38.100
Okay, then. Our ultimate weapon is...

00:09:40.290 --> 00:09:42.220
H-He's not here? He disappeared?

00:09:42.220 --> 00:09:43.040
What?

00:09:43.040 --> 00:09:45.280
It doesn't matter who you choose,
 just hurry up and take your go.

00:09:45.280 --> 00:09:46.940
I want the data.

00:09:46.940 --> 00:09:49.260
T-Timeout, okay?

00:09:49.260 --> 00:09:51.980
Just wait! I'll be right back!

00:09:51.980 --> 00:09:53.650
Ragamen 
Restaurant

00:09:56.610 --> 00:09:59.240
Hirota!

00:09:59.640 --> 00:10:03.650
What are you doing? We're in 
the middle of a tackling contest.

00:10:04.650 --> 00:10:05.600
Not my problem.

00:10:05.600 --> 00:10:09.370
When you're in Sugadaira,
you've gotta have the famous Ragamen.

00:10:09.770 --> 00:10:12.250
But the team's in trouble right now.

00:10:12.250 --> 00:10:14.130
My stomach is in bigger trouble.

00:10:15.920 --> 00:10:19.090
Wait, you didn't hear?

00:10:19.090 --> 00:10:21.400
If we win the tackling contest...

00:10:21.400 --> 00:10:22.860
Whisper, whisper, whisper...

00:10:22.860 --> 00:10:23.850
What?

00:10:23.850 --> 00:10:27.460
You should've said that 
to begin with, idiot!

00:10:28.440 --> 00:10:29.730
Whoops.

00:10:30.440 --> 00:10:34.610
Hey. Since we've got nothing else to do,
let's talk about our love lives, Oharano-kun.

00:10:35.050 --> 00:10:38.200
Are you texting your girlfriend?

00:10:39.530 --> 00:10:41.970
What are you going to do, Jinko?

00:10:41.970 --> 00:10:44.530
It doesn't matter who you choose. 
Just take your turn already.

00:10:47.220 --> 00:10:49.770
Th-Thanks for waiting.

00:10:49.770 --> 00:10:51.540
Hurry up...

00:10:52.070 --> 00:10:56.050
and feed me!

00:10:56.050 --> 00:10:58.050
<b>Score</b>

00:11:03.050 --> 00:11:05.960
Keijo: 556 pounds.

00:11:06.490 --> 00:11:09.650
Sagami: 557 pounds.

00:11:09.650 --> 00:11:12.480
Jinko: 560 pounds.

00:11:14.260 --> 00:11:15.230
How d'you like that?

00:11:15.230 --> 00:11:17.050
The winner is Jinko!

00:11:17.050 --> 00:11:18.740
Feed me!

00:11:18.740 --> 00:11:20.660
Good work, guys.

00:11:19.250 --> 00:11:23.130
That little guy's like an animal trainer.

00:11:23.130 --> 00:11:24.990
You're right.

00:11:24.990 --> 00:11:27.990
<b>This is 
Ragamen!</b>

00:11:24.990 --> 00:11:27.990
Rugby ball-
sized bowl

00:11:24.990 --> 00:11:27.990
950 yen

00:11:27.990 --> 00:11:31.000
<b>Ragamen
 Soup 
Sold Out</b>

00:11:27.990 --> 00:11:31.000
<b>Manager</b>

00:11:31.000 --> 00:11:33.790
<b>Ikuta Inn</b>

00:11:32.270 --> 00:11:33.790
I see.

00:11:33.790 --> 00:11:37.360
No, I'm sorry for making 
an unreasonable request.

00:11:37.360 --> 00:11:38.800
Excuse me.

00:11:43.110 --> 00:11:44.970
Raita!

00:11:51.790 --> 00:11:53.280
Raita!

00:11:53.280 --> 00:11:55.650
Where's Raita?

00:11:57.550 --> 00:11:59.780
Tell him I'm not here. Please.

00:12:00.820 --> 00:12:02.160
What's wrong?

00:12:02.160 --> 00:12:07.520
Raita told me the team would buy me
ice cream if we won that tackling contest,

00:12:07.520 --> 00:12:09.250
that little liar!

00:12:09.250 --> 00:12:10.850
He won't get away with this!

00:12:12.010 --> 00:12:15.040
But you just had dinner. 
You sure do eat a lot.

00:12:15.040 --> 00:12:19.230
The appetite of a chubster and 
culinary grudges know no bounds!

00:12:19.230 --> 00:12:21.630
Raita, where did you go?!

00:12:26.000 --> 00:12:28.050
That was close.

00:12:28.050 --> 00:12:29.320
You've got it bad.

00:12:30.090 --> 00:12:31.390
One hundred.

00:12:31.390 --> 00:12:33.810
Okay, next.

00:12:33.810 --> 00:12:35.600
Gion-kun, where are you going?

00:12:35.600 --> 00:12:38.430
I'm off to do some secret training.

00:12:38.430 --> 00:12:38.860
Bye.

00:12:39.700 --> 00:12:42.450
Have fun with your secret training.

00:12:42.450 --> 00:12:43.740
"Secret"?

00:12:45.240 --> 00:12:50.330
I haven't decided what
my secret training should be yet.

00:12:50.330 --> 00:12:51.510
What should I do?

00:12:54.660 --> 00:12:56.790
Is anyone around?

00:13:11.240 --> 00:13:12.730
G-Gion?

00:13:12.730 --> 00:13:14.810
Senpai, are you doing secret training, too?

00:13:15.500 --> 00:13:17.560
W-Were you watching? I'm so embarrassed.

00:13:17.940 --> 00:13:21.400
That thing you did before
you kicked the ball... Was that for luck?

00:13:27.460 --> 00:13:31.480
It's kind of like a good luck charm
or a prayer.

00:13:31.480 --> 00:13:32.240
A prayer?

00:13:33.250 --> 00:13:37.250
I was on the soccer team in 
elementary and middle school.

00:13:37.250 --> 00:13:38.700
Really?

00:13:39.380 --> 00:13:44.520
I'm not a strong kicker, I lack stamina, 
and I can't produce Hollywood moments.

00:13:45.130 --> 00:13:48.380
I've always been good at predicting 
where the ball will end up,

00:13:49.020 --> 00:13:52.760
but since my body can't keep up 
with my brain, I'm no good in goal.

00:13:52.760 --> 00:13:56.820
And because of my personality, 
I've always been an outcast.

00:13:58.340 --> 00:14:00.770
That sounds familiar.

00:14:01.770 --> 00:14:03.530
I liked it.

00:14:05.100 --> 00:14:07.030
I loved it.

00:14:11.430 --> 00:14:12.490
But it was hard.

00:14:15.900 --> 00:14:18.150
Yeah, I understand.

00:14:19.380 --> 00:14:22.540
Still, I couldn't quit.

00:14:23.160 --> 00:14:28.050
There wasn't anything else I liked,
and I didn't want my teammates to hate me.

00:14:28.050 --> 00:14:31.550
<b>Rugby Club</b>

00:14:29.220 --> 00:14:33.730
I thought I'd keep playing soccer
in high school, but...

00:14:37.520 --> 00:14:41.440
Even after six years, I still didn't belong.

00:14:42.470 --> 00:14:45.750
If this elliptical ball 
started to hate me, too,

00:14:45.750 --> 00:14:50.950
I have a feeling I really wouldn't 
belong anywhere anymore.

00:14:53.270 --> 00:14:56.930
Please... go over.

00:14:58.750 --> 00:15:01.870
It's creepy, isn't it? It's embarrassing.

00:15:01.870 --> 00:15:03.580
I could never do it in front of anyone.

00:15:03.580 --> 00:15:05.500
It's super cool.

00:15:05.500 --> 00:15:06.880
What?

00:15:06.880 --> 00:15:08.870
You don't think it'd weird people out?

00:15:08.870 --> 00:15:12.370
I can kick really calmly when I do it.

00:15:12.370 --> 00:15:14.440
No, it's seriously cool.

00:15:14.440 --> 00:15:16.010
You should do it. I mean it.

00:15:16.350 --> 00:15:17.150
Really?

00:15:18.040 --> 00:15:20.430
But you made your kicks without doing it.

00:15:20.430 --> 00:15:22.520
That's different...

00:15:23.280 --> 00:15:25.020
Nice story.

00:15:25.960 --> 00:15:31.530
Rather than the guys who always
consider things calmly and stoically,

00:15:32.600 --> 00:15:36.220
it's the guys who are desperate
and always afraid of something

00:15:36.220 --> 00:15:38.160
that can be counted on in the clutch.

00:15:39.700 --> 00:15:42.100
And that good luck charm of yours...

00:15:43.420 --> 00:15:45.040
I don't dislike it.

00:15:48.540 --> 00:15:49.210
Catch this!

00:15:49.210 --> 00:15:50.300
What?

00:15:54.340 --> 00:15:55.720
But it's dark.

00:15:55.720 --> 00:15:57.930
I can't see a thing.

00:16:00.320 --> 00:16:01.560
You can't catch it, can you?

00:16:09.450 --> 00:16:10.570
So close!

00:16:11.050 --> 00:16:13.140
You've got good instincts.

00:16:13.140 --> 00:16:14.950
One more, please.

00:16:17.000 --> 00:16:18.450
Gramps, that's amazing.

00:16:20.680 --> 00:16:21.910
What the hell are they doing?

00:16:28.170 --> 00:16:33.200
You were watching the ball closely
in the Tenjiku game.

00:16:33.200 --> 00:16:35.680
Is that what you've been practicing?

00:16:35.680 --> 00:16:39.680
I've always watched people's expressions.

00:16:40.230 --> 00:16:42.930
It's how I know which way 
someone's likely to kick,

00:16:43.300 --> 00:16:46.120
or which way they don't want <i>me</i> to.

00:16:48.200 --> 00:16:51.740
Do you think this kind of practice
will make me better?

00:16:51.740 --> 00:16:53.240
I don't know.

00:16:53.240 --> 00:16:54.600
You don't know?

00:16:54.600 --> 00:16:56.740
I used to do this all the time.

00:16:56.740 --> 00:16:59.990
They'd tell me to use my mind's eye
to catch the ball.

00:17:00.580 --> 00:17:01.350
I caught it.

00:17:03.000 --> 00:17:08.270
Even if you can catch it, there's no telling
if it'll be useful in an actual game.

00:17:08.270 --> 00:17:10.500
It's kind of like a good luck charm, too.

00:17:11.470 --> 00:17:14.230
No one plays in the dark.

00:17:14.230 --> 00:17:17.780
But it makes you feel like 
you've gotten better.

00:17:17.780 --> 00:17:21.770
Yes, sir. But I do have a feeling 
it'll be useful somehow...

00:17:21.770 --> 00:17:25.520
You're wondering what
the mind's eye is, aren't you?

00:17:25.520 --> 00:17:29.200
Yes, sir. But I think I understand.

00:17:29.200 --> 00:17:32.530
He does? This guy's pretty amazing.

00:17:33.010 --> 00:17:37.280
For men like me who lived through times
when guts and machismo were all the rage,

00:17:37.740 --> 00:17:42.290
practice, good luck charms,
and prayers that seemed pointless

00:17:42.290 --> 00:17:44.810
were really important.

00:17:46.410 --> 00:17:50.080
Sorry for making you
listen to me reminiscing.

00:17:50.950 --> 00:17:53.590
It made me happy.

00:17:54.120 --> 00:17:55.510
Thank you, sir.

00:17:57.990 --> 00:17:59.830
Wait a minute!

00:17:59.830 --> 00:18:01.180
Kibi-kun.

00:18:01.180 --> 00:18:04.310
Komori-san, why are you leaving?

00:18:04.310 --> 00:18:05.910
I want to give that a try, too!

00:18:05.910 --> 00:18:08.480
But my hip hurts.

00:18:08.480 --> 00:18:10.130
That's not fair, Kifune!

00:18:10.130 --> 00:18:11.640
You should've invited me!

00:18:11.640 --> 00:18:12.820
S-Sorry.

00:18:15.690 --> 00:18:18.780
Wow, this is seriously hard!

00:18:18.780 --> 00:18:20.400
This is the last one!

00:18:20.960 --> 00:18:23.450
My training...

00:18:23.600 --> 00:18:28.080
Jinko

00:18:23.600 --> 00:18:28.080
Toryo Tech

00:18:25.710 --> 00:18:28.080
Score! We won!

00:18:29.230 --> 00:18:32.590
We'll get yelled at if 
we get carried away again.

00:18:35.840 --> 00:18:39.700
Kibucchi, you didn't miss a single kick!

00:18:39.700 --> 00:18:41.830
Ah, thank you for saying so.

00:18:43.370 --> 00:18:44.850
I made all my tackles, too.

00:18:45.270 --> 00:18:47.820
Is that because of your secret training?

00:18:47.820 --> 00:18:50.250
Y-Yeah, my secret training...

00:18:50.250 --> 00:18:52.110
Boy, I'm hungry.

00:18:52.550 --> 00:18:54.400
Hey, a crêpe place!

00:18:54.400 --> 00:18:56.770
Hey, Tree Trunk. Let's go have one.

00:18:56.770 --> 00:18:59.270
What? But we shouldn't buy sweets now.

00:18:59.270 --> 00:19:01.030
It's almost lunch.

00:19:01.030 --> 00:19:02.660
Who cares?

00:19:02.660 --> 00:19:04.200
Hello.

00:19:05.420 --> 00:19:06.950
Welcome.

00:19:10.620 --> 00:19:12.450
Ryu-chan, it's ready.

00:19:12.450 --> 00:19:13.750
Your "Ryu-chan Special."

00:19:13.750 --> 00:19:14.590
Got it.

00:19:14.590 --> 00:19:19.350
Huh? Ma'am, isn't this 
bigger than last year's?

00:19:19.350 --> 00:19:23.600
Really? Maybe you've gotten 
bigger since last year.

00:19:24.070 --> 00:19:26.930
I'll be in college next year.

00:19:26.930 --> 00:19:29.330
Oh, my. Will you be coming next year, then?

00:19:29.330 --> 00:19:32.950
Yeah, I'll get even bigger and come back.

00:19:32.950 --> 00:19:34.350
You're already big enough!

00:19:35.040 --> 00:19:36.820
It's the giant of Ryoin!

00:19:36.820 --> 00:19:39.600
Ma'am, I'll take a chocolate and banana crêpe.

00:19:39.600 --> 00:19:40.630
What about you?

00:19:40.630 --> 00:19:42.320
I-I'll pass.

00:19:42.320 --> 00:19:45.950
Huh? Have we met somewhere before?

00:19:45.950 --> 00:19:48.830
Yeah, that time you had a stomachache 
from eating too much shaved ice.

00:19:49.260 --> 00:19:51.400
But that happens all the time.

00:19:51.400 --> 00:19:53.090
Ryujin!

00:19:53.630 --> 00:19:56.130
Don't go getting sidetracked.

00:19:56.130 --> 00:19:59.130
I told you we were
heading back for a meeting.

00:20:00.450 --> 00:20:01.630
Sorry, Kota.

00:20:02.130 --> 00:20:04.760
You can have a bite of my Ryu-chan Special.

00:20:04.760 --> 00:20:05.870
I don't want that.

00:20:05.870 --> 00:20:08.770
At least let him have a crêpe, Tsukinaka.

00:20:08.770 --> 00:20:12.050
You guys want some? I'm buying.

00:20:09.870 --> 00:20:12.060
<i>But we just had cake...</i>

00:20:10.080 --> 00:20:11.520
But we just had cake...

00:20:12.060 --> 00:20:13.500
What are you hiding for, Tree Trunk?

00:20:13.500 --> 00:20:14.760
Of course I'm hiding.

00:20:14.760 --> 00:20:17.100
That's Ryoin's captain, Tsukinaka-san.

00:20:17.100 --> 00:20:20.910
And that's the Ryoin team! Who wouldn't hide?

00:20:21.470 --> 00:20:24.590
I'm Gion of Kanagawa High.

00:20:24.590 --> 00:20:26.110
Aren't the twin flankers with you?

00:20:26.110 --> 00:20:27.410
G-Gion-kun.

00:20:27.770 --> 00:20:30.560
Kanagawa High? Gion?

00:20:30.560 --> 00:20:33.190
I think the twins told me about you.

00:20:33.190 --> 00:20:35.420
People call you guys "Jinko," right?

00:20:34.580 --> 00:20:36.540
Come on, come on, come on.

00:20:36.940 --> 00:20:38.610
Don't interfere with our conversation!

00:20:39.720 --> 00:20:42.850
I've heard about you from Keijo's Taira, too.

00:20:42.850 --> 00:20:44.340
Tsukinaka!

00:20:44.790 --> 00:20:47.080
My wallet's missing!

00:20:47.080 --> 00:20:48.350
What are you doing?

00:20:48.350 --> 00:20:51.020
Put that away, Coach!

00:20:51.020 --> 00:20:54.390
I had it when we were eating cake earlier!

00:20:54.390 --> 00:20:56.290
I must've dropped it...

00:20:57.130 --> 00:20:58.610
I'll go check back at the store!

00:20:59.200 --> 00:21:02.750
You dumb coach!

00:21:03.670 --> 00:21:05.300
He's gone.

00:21:08.270 --> 00:21:11.170
Coach, I've got your wallet.

00:21:11.170 --> 00:21:11.870
What?

00:21:11.870 --> 00:21:16.530
You went to the bathroom before 
we left, so I paid for you.

00:21:16.530 --> 00:21:18.380
Oh, right.

00:21:18.380 --> 00:21:20.570
What should we do about Kotaro?

00:21:20.570 --> 00:21:24.380
He's out of sight already. 
I'm going to call him.

00:21:26.510 --> 00:21:28.120
Oh.

00:21:28.120 --> 00:21:29.140
Jeez...

00:21:29.140 --> 00:21:31.120
He's hopeless.

00:21:31.120 --> 00:21:32.890
We're heading back.

00:21:33.220 --> 00:21:35.580
It's a good thing you 
found your wallet, Coach.

00:21:35.580 --> 00:21:37.040
Yeah, thank goodness!

00:21:37.040 --> 00:21:39.200
The twins aren't with you?

00:21:39.200 --> 00:21:42.780
They already left. Sorry.

00:21:43.430 --> 00:21:46.780
Uh, um, Coach...

00:21:46.780 --> 00:21:48.490
Excuse me.

00:21:48.490 --> 00:21:52.240
I'm the Kanagawa High team's advisor.

00:21:52.240 --> 00:21:53.830
My name's Yoshida.

00:21:53.830 --> 00:21:55.080
Yoshida-sensei?

00:21:55.080 --> 00:22:01.380
Oh, Kanagawa High? 
I'm Ryoin's coach, Minamoto.

00:22:01.380 --> 00:22:02.800
Nice to meet you.

00:22:02.800 --> 00:22:09.970
I know this is sudden, but would you 
be willing to play us in two days' time?

00:23:44.980 --> 00:23:49.990
<b>Next Time: "Your Turf"</b>

00:23:46.010 --> 00:23:48.860
Next time: "Your Turf."
